                <pb facs="0245" n="145" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg145"/>

                <head>No. 132.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hunter to Mr. Seward.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-11-07"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 7,
                        1879</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 321.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: You will please report upon the judicial
                    systems of the United States, Great Britain, and France in China, and will
                    accompany such report with copies of the court rules and form of procedure in
                    force under such systems.</p>
                <p>It is desired that your report shall fully cover the grounds so as to give the
                    Department a clear view of the various systems in force, and you may, if you
                    think proper, present for the consideration of the Department in this connection
                    any suggestions for the improvement of our system which may occur to you.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. HUNTER.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
